---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ActivityStream from "../components/ActivityStream.astro";

const columns = [
  ["activity_id", "A stable identifier for the event record."],
  ["ts", "The UTC timestamp when the event happened."],
  ["customer", "The entity that performed or experienced the activity."],
  ["activity", "A clear verb phrase such as completed_order."],
  ["feature_json", "Activity-specific context such as plan, campaign, or product."],
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Activities — Activity Schema"
  description="Learn how Activity Schema models independent business events in a consistent, warehouse-native activity stream."
  path="/activities/"
>
  <header class="page-hero shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">The modeling unit</p>
    <h1>Model what the business does.</h1>
    <p class="lede">An activity is a clear business event: a customer <strong>opened an email</strong>, a company <strong>signed a contract</strong>, or an order <strong>was shipped</strong>.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="section-tight">
    <div class="shell example-wrap">
      <ActivityStream />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell content-grid">
      <aside>
        <p class="eyebrow">Core idea</p>
        <p class="aside-copy">One activity. One definition. One place to inspect and maintain it.</p>
      </aside>
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Every row tells the same kind of story.</h2>
        <p>At its simplest, an Activity Schema describes an entity taking an action at a point in time. The fixed structure is what makes the model discoverable: once you understand one activity, you know how to approach all of them.</p>
        <p>The specification supports one shared stream table—the preferred default—or one table per activity when warehouse performance makes that useful.</p>
        <div class="column-list">
          {columns.map(([name, description]) => (
            <div>
              <code>{name}</code>
              <p>{description}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-rule">
    <div class="shell content-grid">
      <aside>
        <p class="eyebrow">Good definitions</p>
        <p class="aside-copy">Prefer stable business language over source-system language.</p>
      </aside>
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Make the name useful on its own.</h2>
        <p>A good activity is independently meaningful. It describes something that actually happened, uses a past-tense verb, and does not hide a chain of unrelated logic.</p>
        <div class="do-dont grid-2">
          <article class="card good">
            <span class="flag">Clear activities</span>
            <code>started_subscription</code>
            <code>opened_support_ticket</code>
            <code>received_shipment</code>
          </article>
          <article class="card weak">
            <span class="flag">Harder to reuse</span>
            <code>customer_status_table</code>
            <code>marketing_funnel_v4</code>
            <code>final_orders_report</code>
          </article>
        </div>
        <p>The second group names artifacts rather than business events. Those artifacts tend to encode one audience or question; activities stay useful as questions change.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section code-section">
    <div class="shell content-grid">
      <aside>
        <p class="eyebrow">Build one</p>
        <p class="aside-copy">Transform the source directly into the standard shape.</p>
      </aside>
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Keep the transformation close to its source.</h2>
        <p>This simplified example defines one activity. Real implementations should also follow the identifier, feature, and incremental-processing guidance in the specification.</p>
        <pre aria-label="SQL example creating a completed order activity"><code><span class="keyword">select</span>
  cast(order_id <span class="keyword">as</span> varchar) <span class="keyword">as</span> activity_id,
  completed_at                   <span class="keyword">as</span> ts,
  cast(customer_id <span class="keyword">as</span> varchar) <span class="keyword">as</span> customer,
  <span class="string">'completed_order'</span>               <span class="keyword">as</span> activity,
  json_object(
    <span class="string">'plan'</span>, plan_name,
    <span class="string">'channel'</span>, acquisition_channel
  )                              <span class="keyword">as</span> feature_json,
  order_total                    <span class="keyword">as</span> revenue_impact
<span class="keyword">from</span> source.orders
<span class="keyword">where</span> completed_at <span class="keyword">is not null</span>;</code></pre>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button button-primary" href="https://github.com/ActivitySchema/ActivitySchema/blob/main/2.0.md#activity-stream">Read the required columns <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          <a class="button button-secondary" href="/temporal-joins/">Next: combine activities</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .example-wrap {
    max-width: 920px;
  }

  .content-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 250px minmax(0, 760px);
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 72px;
  }

  .aside-copy {
    max-width: 220px;
    color: var(--steel);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .column-list {
    margin-block: 40px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .column-list > div {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 150px 1fr;
    gap: 24px;
    padding-block: 18px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .column-list p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }

  .do-dont {
    margin-block: 36px;
  }

  .do-dont article {
    display: grid;
    gap: 12px;
    padding: 22px;
  }

  .do-dont .good {
    border-top: 3px solid var(--seafoam);
  }

  .do-dont .weak {
    border-top: 3px solid var(--fog);
  }

  .flag {
    margin-bottom: 10px;
    color: var(--steel);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  pre {
    overflow-x: auto;
    margin-block: 36px;
    padding: 28px;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--midnight);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);
    color: #d9dee2;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  pre code {
    color: inherit;
  }

  .keyword {
    color: var(--seafoam);
  }

  .string {
    color: var(--seafoam-light);
  }

  .code-section {
    background: var(--white);
  }

  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .content-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 28px;
    }

    .aside-copy {
      max-width: 520px;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .column-list > div {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 6px;
    }
  }
</style>
